# Content quality

## Voice
- Human, contractor-practical. Short sentences. Prefer “enter length × width” over abstract marketing.
- **Banned filler:** “in today’s world”, “delve”, “it’s important to note”, “whether you’re a beginner or a pro”, “look no further”, “unlock”, “elevate”, “comprehensive guide to”, “game-changer”, “leverage”, “robust solution”, emoji-heavy intros.
- No fake first-person job-site stories. No invented credentials.

## Facts
- **No invented stats.** Every number (bag yield, coverage, density, seeding rate, pitch factor) needs a primary source link (manufacturer TDS or extension).
- Prefer QUIKRETE/Sakrete/BEHR/IKO/GAF TDS and university extension (e.g. Iowa PM 1072, UMN, Penn State) over blogs.
- Label rules of thumb as such; tell readers to confirm the bag/can/code.

## Page trust chrome
- Guides: visible **Sources** list + byline `Reviewed by Hammad Iqbal · Last updated {date}` (see `guides/[slug].astro`).
- Tools: `TrustBlock` Sources list + last reviewed date matching `dateModified`.
- Bump `dateModified` only when content/math actually changed — never set sitemap lastmod to “now”.

## Structure (guides)
- Answer-first 40–60 words with a sourced number/verdict in sentence 1 when one exists.
- Question-style H2s from real PAA/search questions.
- Worked example with real numbers; FAQ 3–5 items; ≥800 words unique body in `guideBodies.ts`.

## Structure (tools)
- Answer-first 40–60 words before inputs; calculator above the fold.
- SSR default worked-example results (no em-dash placeholders) via `src/data/calculatorFields.ts`.
- FAQ 3–5 sourced items; link ≥1 topical guide.
